# The Xray core CasaVPN runs, pinned separately from the one 3x-ui bundles.
# install.sh and upgrade.sh read this file (parsed, never sourced), download the
# official XTLS/Xray-core release zip, refuse it unless its SHA-256 matches, and
# put its `xray` binary over /usr/local/x-ui/bin/xray-linux-<arch>. The core
# 3x-ui shipped is kept next to it as xray-linux-<arch>.bundled.
#
# WHY THE PIN EXISTS: Xray 26.10.10, the core bundled with 3x-ui 3.10.2, rejects
# Shadowrocket (iOS) at the Reality handshake ("REALITY: processed invalid
# connection ... authentication failed or validation criteria not met"), while
# Xray-based clients and an old 26.2.6 test client keep working. Keys, shortId,
# SNI, clock and minClientVer were all correct; running 26.7.28 with the same
# 3x-ui fixed it. The root cause inside 26.10.10 is not known. Leave the pin
# alone until a newer core has been tested with Shadowrocket on mobile data
# (docs/UPGRADING.md, "Changing the Xray core").
#
# To move the pin, change all three hashes and the version in one commit. The
# hashes come from the release's .dgst files (SHA2-256=) and match the asset
# digests that `gh release view <tag> -R XTLS/Xray-core --json assets` prints.
# Opt out of the pin on one host with CASAVPN_XRAY_CORE=bundled in casavpn.env.
XRAY_CORE_VERSION=v26.7.28
XRAY_CORE_SHA256_AMD64=8195d909f1109b8f3d99eefe401a3c451d7bf4af71f24d3815420f77e5dd2a40
XRAY_CORE_SHA256_ARM64=f5698bb218ada3b4022db26fafc39601c5f53b46b19eb76c9616325985807501
XRAY_CORE_REPO=XTLS/Xray-core
